","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Hailong","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Kaixin","key":"yangkaixinpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Kaixin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Peibo","key":"shipeibopau","last":"Shi","name":"Shi, Peibo","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Zhipeng","key":"zhangzhipengpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Zhipeng","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Qikai","key":"fengqikaipau","last":"Feng","name":"Feng, Qikai","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","first":"Carol Vannesa","key":"nawenjacarolvannesapau","last":"Nawenja","name":"Nawenja, Carol Vannesa","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Vincent","key":"obandavincentpau","last":"Obanda","name":"Obanda, Vincent","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Kityo","key":"robertkityopau","last":"Robert","name":"Robert, Kityo","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Betty","key":"nalikkabettypau","last":"Nalikka","name":"Nalikka, Betty","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Cecilia Njeri","key":"waruhiucecilianjeripau","last":"Waruhiu","name":"Waruhiu, Cecilia Njeri","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 7","first":"Griphin Ochieng","key":"ocholagriphinochiengpau","last":"Ochola","name":"Ochola, Griphin Ochieng","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 7","first":"Samson Omondi","key":"onyuoksamsonomondipau","last":"Onyuok","name":"Onyuok, Samson Omondi","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 7","first":"Harold","key":"ochiengharoldpau","last":"Ochieng","name":"Ochieng, Harold","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Bei","key":"libeipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Bei","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Yan","key":"zhuyanpau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Yan","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Haorui","key":"sihaoruipau","last":"Si","name":"Si, Haorui","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jiefang","key":"yinjiefangpau","last":"Yin","name":"Yin, Jiefang","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"Karsten","key":"kristiansenkarstenpau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"941041b1-1b8f-4be5-9a65-5e98f662c07e","name":"Kristiansen, Karsten","orcid":"0000-0002-6024-0917","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xin","key":"jinxinpau","last":"Jin","name":"Jin, Xin","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xun","key":"xuxunpau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Xun","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Minfeng","key":"xiaominfengpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Minfeng","rank":25,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","first":"Bernard","key":"agwandabernardpau","last":"Agwanda","name":"Agwanda, Bernard","rank":26,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","first":"Sheila","key":"ommehsheilapau","last":"Ommeh","name":"Ommeh, Sheila","rank":27,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Junhua","key":"lijunhuapau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Junhua","rank":28,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 10","first":"Zheng Li","key":"shizhenglipau","last":"Shi","name":"Shi, Zheng Li","rank":29,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38600530"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s40168-024-01782-4","issn":["20492618"],"issue":"1","journal":"Microbiome","paperid":"72","status":"p","title":"Microbiome","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85189888408"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-23e461ae-9374-4394-8a1b-a5839f5033e5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Substantial viral diversity in bats and rodents from East Africa : insights into evolution, recombination, and cocirculation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730634","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Nanotechnology has a wide range of applications, and the pollution and toxicity of their overuse must also be taken seriously. The dual effects of cerium oxide nanoparticles (CeO2 NPs) on alfalfa (Medicago sativa L.) through regulating programmed cell death (PCD) were investigated. Herein, foliar spray of CeO2 NPs on alfalfa revealed a dose-dependent effect of CeO2 NPs. CeO2 NPs at low concentrations had a positive effect but those at high concentrations had phytotoxicity. Specifically, 100 mg L−1 CeO2 NPs improved the morphology, biomass, pigments, photosynthesis, stomatal opening, ultrastructure, osmotic and redox homeostasis, the antioxidant enzyme and the anti-PCD genes, and several hormones, accompanied by lower PCD-promoting gene expression and cellular features. Conversely, 1000 mg L−1 CeO2 NPs induced PCD by causing oxidative damage, along with negative morphology, reduced quality, high Ce accumulation, weak photosynthesis, stomatal closure, lipid peroxidation, apoptosis, impaired cellular ultrastructure, DNA fragmentation, osmotic and redox instability, gene alterations, and hormonal fluctuations. Overall, alfalfa responds to the duality of CeO2 NPs by controlling PCD, which is regulated by a complex network. This study proposes a fresh outlook on the rational utilization of CeO2 NPs, the promotion of sustainable agriculture, and the prevention of environmental pollution caused by nanomaterials.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Chen, Zhao","Guo, Zhipeng","Xu, Nan","Khan, Md Zulfikar","Niu, Junpeng"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-745563"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Niu, Junpeng"],"country":["China","France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","L'Institut Agro Rennes-Angers","Northwest Agriculture and Forestry University","Yangzhou University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multiple insights into the two sided effects of foliar application of cerium oxide nanoparticles on the growth of alfalfa i medicago sativa i l","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85197513559","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-745563","identifier":[{"id":"85197513559","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-e261a616-c3a4-45bb-95cb-43579149e8a1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5367F5398EDCE0A934E6F603CC3C3784"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"yangzhou university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Yangzhou University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"northwest agriculture and forestry university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Northwest Agriculture and Forestry University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Climate and Water"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"fr","key":"l institut agro rennes angers","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"L'Institut Agro Rennes-Angers","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhao","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Zhao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhipeng","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Zhipeng","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nan","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","locid":"8e088f5b-93dd-481e-b437-54f76e61d1fc","name":"Xu, Nan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Md Zulfikar","key":"khanpau","last":"Khan","name":"Khan, Md Zulfikar","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Junpeng","key":"niupau","last":"Niu","name":"Niu, Junpeng","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1039/d4en00271g","issn":["20518153","20518161"],"issn_org":["20518153"],"issue":"8","journal":"Environmental Science: Nano","pages":"3457-3474","publisher":"Royal Society of Chemistry","status":"p","title":"Environmental Science: Nano","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85197513559"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e261a616-c3a4-45bb-95cb-43579149e8a1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Multiple insights into the two-sided effects of foliar application of cerium oxide nanoparticles on the growth of alfalfa (<i>Medicago sativa </i>L.)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-745563","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The availability of large-scale datasets, advanced architectures, and powerful computational resources have led to effective code models that automate diverse software engineering activities. The datasets usually consist of billions of lines of code from both open-source and private repositories. A code model memorizes and produces source code verbatim, which potentially contains vulnerabilities, sensitive information, or code with strict licenses, leading to potential security and privacy issues. This paper investigates an important problem: to what extent do code models memorize their training data? We conduct an empirical study to explore memorization in large pre-trained code models. Our study highlights that simply extracting 20,000 outputs (each having 512 tokens) from a code model can produce over 40,125 code snippets that are memorized from the training data. To provide a better understanding, we build a taxonomy of memorized contents with 3 categories and 14 subcategories. The results show that the prompts sent to the code models affect the distribution of memorized contents. We identify several key factors of memorization. Specifically, given the same architecture, larger models suffer more from memorization problem. A code model produces more memorization when it is allowed to generate longer outputs. We also find a strong positive correlation between the number of an output's occurrences in the training data and that in the generated outputs, which indicates that a potential way to reduce memorization is to remove duplicates in the training data. We then identify effective metrics that infer whether an output contains memorization accurately. We also make suggestions to deal with memorization.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Yang, Zhou","Zhao, Zhipeng","Wang, Chenyu","Shi, Jieke","Kim, Dongsun","Han, Donggyun","Lo, David"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-748132"],"event":{"end":"2024-04-20","place":"Lisbon, pt","start":"2024-04-14","title":"44th ACM/IEEE International Conference on Software Engineering, ICSE 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, South","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Singapore","South Korea","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Kyungpook National University","Royal Holloway University of London","Singapore Management University"],"keyword":["Code generation","Open source software","Security and privacy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"unveiling memorization in code models","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3597503.3639074","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-748132","identifier":[{"id":"85196836859","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-5a86703c-743d-4d22-8a26-95be84e9c872"],"keyword":["Code Generation","Computing methodologies → Artificial intelligence","Memorization","Open-Source Software","Security and privacy","Software and its engineering → Software development techniques"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-512BC614ED036E5822412C1979F62ADC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3597503.3639074","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/396994826/Unveiling_Memorization_in_Code_Models.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"sg","key":"singapore management university","loc":["Singapore","Asia, South"],"name":"Singapore Management University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"kr","key":"kyungpook national university","loc":["South Korea","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Kyungpook National University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"royal holloway university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Royal Holloway University of London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Zhou","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Zhou","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Zhipeng","key":"zhaopau","last":"Zhao","locid":"e5c18578-ae38-4581-87a8-8093763d3b75","name":"Zhao, Zhipeng","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Chenyu","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Chenyu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jieke","key":"shipau","last":"Shi","name":"Shi, Jieke","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Dongsun","key":"kimpau","last":"Kim","name":"Kim, Dongsun","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Donggyun","key":"hanpau","last":"Han","name":"Han, Donggyun","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"David","key":"lopau","last":"Lo","name":"Lo, David","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3597503.3639074","eisbn":["9798400702174"],"pages":"867-879","publisher":"IEEE Computer Society Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings - 2024 ACM/IEEE 44th International Conference on Software Engineering, ICSE 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85196836859"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5a86703c-743d-4d22-8a26-95be84e9c872"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Unveiling Memorization in Code Models","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-748132","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Leveraging large-scale datasets from open-source projects and advances in large language models, recent progress has led to sophisticated code models for key software engineering tasks, such as program repair and code completion. These models are trained on data from various sources, including public open-source projects like GitHub and private, confidential code from companies, raising significant privacy concerns. This paper investigates a crucial but unexplored question: What is the risk of membership information leakage in code models? Membership leakage refers to the vulnerability where an attacker can infer whether a specific data point was part of the training dataset. We present GOTCHA, a novel membership inference attack method designed for code models, and evaluate its effectiveness on Java-based datasets. G OTCHA simultaneously considers three key factors: model input, model output, and ground truth. Our ablation study confirms that each factor significantly enhances attack performance. Our ablation study confirms that each factor significantly enhances attack performance. Our investigation reveals a troubling finding: membership leakage risk is significantly elevated. While previous methods had accuracy close to random guessing, G OTCHA achieves high precision, with a true positive rate of 0.95 and a low false positive rate of 0.10. We also demonstrate that the attacker's knowledge of the victim model (e.g., model architecture and pre-training data) affects attack success. Additionally, modifying decoding strategies can help reduce membership leakage risks. This research highlights the urgent need to better understand the privacy vulnerabilities of code models and develop strong countermeasures against these threats.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Yang, Zhou","Zhao, Zhipeng","Wang, Chenyu","Shi, Jieke","Kim, Dongsun","Han, Dong Gyun","Lo, David"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-777284"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, South","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Singapore","South Korea","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Kyungpook National University","Royal Holloway University of London","Singapore Management University"],"keyword":["Membership Inference Attack","Privacy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gotcha this model uses my code evaluating membership leakage risks in code models","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/414763907/Gotcha_This_Model_Uses_My_Code_Evaluating.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-777284","identifier":[{"id":"85207929323","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-2c981428-84e3-4b99-8b96-3298f4a99ba4"],"keyword":["Code Completion","Large Langauge Models for Code","Membership Inference Attack","Privacy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-25D9925FB25EF9F6CEF7D0A6D931CFBF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/414763907/Gotcha_This_Model_Uses_My_Code_Evaluating.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"sg","key":"singapore management university","loc":["Singapore","Asia, South"],"name":"Singapore Management University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"kr","key":"kyungpook national university","loc":["South Korea","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Kyungpook National University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"royal holloway university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Royal Holloway University of London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Zhou","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Zhou","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Zhipeng","key":"zhaopau","last":"Zhao","locid":"e5c18578-ae38-4581-87a8-8093763d3b75","name":"Zhao, Zhipeng","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Chenyu","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Chenyu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jieke","key":"shipau","last":"Shi","name":"Shi, Jieke","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Dongsun","key":"kimpau","last":"Kim","name":"Kim, Dongsun","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Dong Gyun","key":"hanpau","last":"Han","name":"Han, Dong Gyun","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"David","key":"lopau","last":"Lo","name":"Lo, David","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tse.2024.3482719","issn":["00985589","19393520"],"issn_org":["00985589"],"issue":"8","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Software Engineering","pages":"3290-3306","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Software Engineering","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85207929323"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2c981428-84e3-4b99-8b96-3298f4a99ba4"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Gotcha! This Model Uses My Code! Evaluating Membership Leakage Risks in Code Models","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-777284","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The rumen is the hallmark organ of ruminants and hosts a diverse ecosystem of microorganisms that facilitates efficient digestion of plant fibers. We analyzed 897 transcriptomes from three Cetartiodactyla lineages: ruminants, camels and cetaceans, as well as data from ruminant comparative genomics and functional assays to explore the genetic basis of rumen functional innovations. We identified genes with relatively high expression in the rumen, of which many appeared to be recruited from other tissues. These genes show functional enrichment in ketone body metabolism, regulation of microbial community, and epithelium absorption, which are the most prominent biological processes involved in rumen innovations. Several modes of genetic change underlying rumen functional innovations were uncovered, including coding mutations, genes newly evolved, and changes of regulatory elements. We validated that the key ketogenesis rate-limiting gene (HMGCS2) with five ruminant-specific mutations was under positive selection and exhibits higher synthesis activity than those of other mammals. Two newly evolved genes (LYZ1 and DEFB1) are resistant to Gram-positive bacteria and thereby may regulate microbial community equilibrium. Furthermore, we confirmed that the changes of regulatory elements accounted for the majority of rumen gene recruitment. These results greatly improve our understanding of rumen evolution and organ evo-devo in general.","author_count":40,"contributors":["Pan, Xiangyu","Cai, Yudong","Li, Zongjun","Chen, Xianqing","Heller, Rasmus","Wang, Nini","Wang, Yu","Zhao, Chen","Wang, Yong","Xu, Han","Li, Songhai","Li, Ming","Li, Cunyuan","Hu, Shengwei","Li, Hui","Wang, Kun","Chen, Lei","Wei, Bin","Zheng, Zhuqing","Fu, Weiwei","Yang, Yue","Zhang, Tingting","Hou, Zhuoting","Yan, Yueyang","Lv, Xiaoyang","Sun, Wei","Li, Xinyu","Huang, Shisheng","Liu, Lixiang","Mao, Shengyong","Liu, Wenqing","Hua, Jinlian","Li, Zhipeng","Zhang, Guojie","Chen, Yulin","Wang, Xihong",